Title: Gaze seats as detached headless CLIs: no nesting limit, cross-family by default
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-27T11:21Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Author ruling, 2026-10-27 (option C of the raid's gaze discussion; A and B went into ticket 1241).
In today's raid every hunt-run gaze degraded to a same-identity self-read: the coder runs at subagent
depth 1 and gaze's seats would need depth 2, which the runtime refused ("seats could not launch
(nesting limit)", PR #1736). 1241 makes gaze say so (`self-only`) and raises Claude Code's depth.
That does not reach Codex or Pi, and every seat stays Anthropic-family inside Claude Code.
`skills/raid/references/detached-gaze.md` and `skills/gaze/references/panel.md` § Detached-seat
substitution already describe a headless seat (`claude -p`, `codex exec -m`, `pi -p`) with containment rails.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Gaze can launch each seat as a detached headless CLI on all three runtimes, with the model
      pinned per seat from the route skill, the containment rails of panel.md, and a bounded wait.
- [ ] A seat from another model family is the default for the review perspective that risk calls
      for (`skills/route/references/decorrelation.md`), and the seat line records family and model.
- [ ] A seat that cannot launch is reported as missing, never replaced by a self-read.
- [ ] Spending on another provider's model is declared in the plan before launch (author consent
      to cross-family spend recorded once, in config, not per run).
- [ ] The harness gate passes; the subagent path keeps working.

## Relevant files
skills/gaze/references/panel.md, skills/gaze/SKILL.md, skills/raid/references/detached-gaze.md,
skills/route/routes.json (launch_doors), scripts/gaze_setup.py, scripts/gaze_close.py

Related: [[1241]], [[1252]].
